ience not being able to  speak as fast and and be as sharp as i  used to  that is definitely something that is  concerning to me  i was very fit and healthy before i  contracted the virus  before the spring i was with my  partner's family  in norway and we were hiking up  mountains  on the west coast the most worrying  thing  through all of this has been they  haven't been able to find a reason  for why i've been so poorly  [Music]  i'm about to get on zoom with pastor  robert dixon  post covet symptoms how's everything  going with that how are you making it  through it's been a pleasure  just knowing somebody else like you're  not on the island by yourself  when i saw you put your um facebook post  up  about you dealing with covet and just  the extent  of how you went into details it was  really  good to hear and then it helped me to be  able to  share more about what i was dealing with  if i'm in the middle of a thought  i can be thinking of the word and just  will not get it right that's me  yes absolutely in regards to  preventing further decline i don't know  if there's anything that we can do  mostly because i don't think we  understand enough about the time course  and the ideology or the cause of these  symptoms  i fear that they will never get back to  baseline  we can't tell for now whether that's a  possibility or not  just had a heart episode coming down the  stairs my heart hit  150 beats per minute  i'm out of breath another trip to urgent  care  waiting to find out if we're gonna have  to go to the er or not  had another heart episode yesterday and  this morning  [Music]  everything that i'm doing now is to  get my body my mind back  to where i was before i don't want to  stay in the place that i'm in right now  because it's not a good place  mentally emotionally or physically  i exercise in the mornings i may not be  able to do  the full 30 minute workout but  i'll try to do something just for the  sake of saying that i that i am  continuing working 